{
  "type": "record",
  "name": "PaymentStatusChanged",
  "namespace": "com.example.psp.common.events.avro",
  "doc": "Avro form of payments.payment-status-changed.v1 (M9 Phase 2). Field-for-field identical to the hand-written psp-connector adapters.out.kafka.PaymentStatusChanged / ledger adapters.in.kafka.PaymentStatusChangedEvent / webhook-notifier adapters.in.kafka.PaymentStatusChangedEvent records this schema replaces - three services (psp-connector produces, ledger and webhook-notifier's planner both consume) move together in this one phase, which is why this is 'the important one' per the M9 Phase 2 brief. Registered under Schema Registry subject 'payments.payment-status-changed.v1-value' (TopicNameStrategy, ADR-0001) - stays v1, cut in place; see services/psp-connector/README.md's M9 Phase 2 section for why this did not need a v2 topic despite having two independent consumer groups, and for the drain-to-latest strategy used to avoid poison-pilling the pre-existing JSON backlog.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "envelope",
      "type": "com.example.psp.common.events.avro.EventEnvelope"
    },
    {
      "name": "paymentId",
      "type": "string",
      "doc": "The payment this status change is about; also envelope.aggregateId (ADR-0002) - NOT the record key. See KafkaPaymentStatusPublisher for the key."
    },
    {
      "name": "merchantId",
      "type": "string",
      "doc": "The owning merchant; IS the record key (ADR-0003) - deliberately different from payments.payment-requested.v1's paymentId key, so every status change for one merchant lands on one partition in order (the ledger's single-writer-per-balance invariant, M7)."
    },
    {
      "name": "amount",
      "type": {
        "type": "bytes",
        "logicalType": "decimal",
        "precision": 19,
        "scale": 4
      },
      "doc": "Generates java.math.BigDecimal (enableDecimalLogicalType=true)."
    },
    {
      "name": "currency",
      "type": "string",
      "doc": "ISO-4217 three-letter currency code."
    },
    {
      "name": "status",
      "type": "string",
      "doc": "Full vocabulary (M21): 'PENDING' (accepted for processing, pre-provider) -> 'IPN_RECEIVED' (provider responded) -> 'VERIFIED' (M5 dedup cleared, genuinely new work) -> 'SUCCEEDED'/'DECLINED' (terminal). PENDING/IPN_RECEIVED/VERIFIED are non-terminal trail stages, history-only downstream; never emitted for a TIMEOUT outcome (ADR-0006 category A is not a business outcome). PENDING carries providerReference=\"\" - no provider call has happened yet; every other status carries the provider's real event id."
    },
    {
      "name": "providerReference",
      "type": "string",
      "doc": "The (simulated) provider's own event id for this attempt (UUID string form) - always present, even on a decline (domain.model.ProviderResult's javadoc). The same value persisted as provider_event_id in psp-connector's dedup table."
    },
    {
      "name": "declineReason",
      "type": ["null", "string"],
      "default": null,
      "doc": "Populated only when status = 'DECLINED', else null."
    }
  ]
}
